To work with a Promise, you can use the `.then()` method to specify a callback function that will be called when the promise is fulfilled:
```
promise.then((result) => {
  console.log(result); // prints "Hello, world!"
});
```
Alternatively, you can use the `.catch()` method to specify a callback function that will be called when the promise is rejected:
```
promise.catch((error) => {
  console.error(error); // prints the error message
});
```
You can also use the `.finally()` method to specify a callback function that will be called regardless of whether the promise is fulfilled or rejected:
```
promise.finally(() => {
  console.log("Done!"); // prints "Done!"
});
```
